2. Create a subscription plan: You can set up a subscription plan in Stripe that corresponds to your membership product. This will ensure that the customer is charged annually for their membership.
3. Add a product exchange feature: You can add a custom plugin or code to your website that allows customers to exchange products within the membership period. This plugin will trigger a new product order and adjust the subscription price accordingly.
4. Set up a renewal reminder: On the fifth month of the membership period, you can send a reminder to customers that they have the option to exchange their product.
5. Implement a cancellation policy: You will also need to have a clear cancellation policy in place, so that customers can cancel their membership or subscription if they wish.

