user said, "I want to keep a record of all products the user have purchased and delink with the current product and link with the new product"
assistant said, "To keep a record of all products the user has purchased and delink them with the current product and link them with the new product, you can use the WooCommerce order notes functionality. When the user exchanges the product, you can add a new order note to the original order with the details of the exchanged product. Here's how you can modify the `exchange_product()` function to add an order note:
```php
function exchange_product() {
    if (isset($_POST['exchange_product'])) {
        $order_id = $_POST['order_id'];
        $product_id = $_POST['product_id'];
        $new_product_id = $_POST['new_product_id'];
        $order = wc_get_order($order_id);
        $order_item = $order->get_item($product_id);
        $order_item->update_meta_data('_product_id', $new_product_id);
        $order->calculate_totals();
        $order->save();

        // Add a new order note with the details of the exchanged product
        $note = sprintf(__('Product exchanged from "%s" to "%s".', 'textdomain'), get_the_title($product_id), get_the_title($new_product_id));
        $order->add_order_note($note);
    }
}
add_action('init', 'exchange_product');
```
This will add an order note to the original order with the details of the exchanged product, which you can view on the order edit screen in the WooCommerce admin area. This will allow you to keep a record of all products the user has purchased and exchanged during their membership."
